# fy-conformance test corpus
#
# Schema: see fy_conformance/dataset.py
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are skipped by the loader.
#
# Categories:
#   - param_validation_auto    : BV/EC for OpenAI numeric params (most regression value)
#   - param_validation_manual  : structural negatives (missing/empty/null fundamentals)
#   - messages_structure       : message array shape
#   - openai_features          : non-mandatory OpenAI features (logprobs/response_format/etc.)
#   - tools                    : function-calling validation
#   - reasoning                : reasoning_effort + thinking parameter
#   - anthropic_messages       : /v1/messages negatives — protocol layer (universal),
#                                with a few claude-only sub-cases for thinking/cache_control
#   - auth                     : Authorization header
#   - malformed                : malformed request bodies
#
# applies_to_backends omitted = applies to all. Otherwise the run is
# scoped: only cases whose list contains target.backend will run.
#
# expect_status_class accepts: 2xx | 4xx | 5xx | 4xx_or_5xx | 2xx_or_4xx.
# Use 2xx_or_4xx when 'either is acceptable; 5xx is the only failure'
# (i.e. range/semantic checks where Claude tolerates and OpenAI rejects).
